For any  $x\in V_i$ and $y\in V_{3-i}$  there exist at least two alternating walks from $x$ to $y$ of length at most $L$, one starting with a blue edge and another starting with a red edge.

	For  $w \in V_1 \cup V_2$ and an integer $k \ge 1$, define $R^w_k$ and $B^w_k$ as  the sets of vertices $v\in V(F)$ such that there is an alternating walk from $v$ to $w$ of length $\ell \le k$, $\ell\equiv k \pmod{2}$, starting with, respectively, a red edge and a blue edge.
(Note that these definitions concern walks {\em ending} with $w$.)

